_unknown='ignore') fitted on training data", "meaning": "Represents categorical differences without imposing order.", "automatic": false, "decision": "APPROVED (executed in preprocessing encoder)"}, {"id": "FEAT-016", "name": "centered_numeric_predictors", "group": "Inferential", "formula": "x - training mean", "meaning": "Makes the intercept and interaction terms interpretable.", "automatic": false, "decision": "USE WHEN POLYNOMIAL OR INTERACTION TERMS ENTER"}], "governance": {"audit_events": 21, "lineage_nodes": 3, "approved_features": 10, "approved_predictors": 19, "decisions": [{"decision": "Restrict the model catalogue to the linear family (LinearRegression, Ridge, Lasso).", "rationale": "Team decision favouring transparent, defensible, coefficient-interpretable models for a managerial audience; the catalogue stays extensible so ensembles can be added later."}, {"decision": "Split into train/validation/test early; the test split is untouched until a single final evaluation of the champion.", "rationale": "Professor's explicit doctrine; prevents optimistic bias and information leakage into model selection."}, {"decision": "Impute missing total_bedrooms with the median fitted on the training split only, after the split.", "rationale": "Prevents leakage of validation/test information into the imputation statistic."}, {"decision": "Tune Ridge/Lasso alpha on the dedicated validation split rather than k-fold cross-validation over train+validation.", "rationale": "Respects the professor's train/validation/test doctrine; keeps selection and final testing strictly separated."}, {"decision": "Training refuses any model not present in model_approval.json; features not approved are excluded from the modelling matrix.", "rationale": "Enforces the approval workflow so only governed, human-approved artifacts reach production."}]}, "stages": [{"n": 1, "name": "Project Management", "desc": "Define objectives, stakeholders, configuration and metadata for the housing-valuation project.", "outputs": "project registry, config"}, {"n": 2, "name": "Data Ingestion", "desc": "Download the California Housing dataset from Kaggle and store an immutable raw copy.", "outputs": "data/raw/housing.csv (20,640 rows)"}, {"n": 3, "name": "Data Understanding", "desc": "Profile every variable against a human-approved semantic schema; quantify missingness, ranges, skew.", "outputs": "validation report, variable summary"}, {"n": 4, "name": "Preprocessing", "desc": "Clean, then split EARLY (stratified on income, seed 42) so the test set stays untouched; impute/scale fit on TRAIN only.", "outputs": "train/validation/test splits"}, {"n": 5, "name": "Feature Engineering", "desc": "Propose features in five governed groups, approve only leakage-safe ones, then execute (6 ratios + 4 log transforms).", "outputs": "10 approved engineered features"}, {"n": 6, "name": "Model Proposal", "desc": "Restrict the catalogue to the interpretable linear family and record the approval decision.", "outputs": "model_proposal.json, approvals"}, {"n": 7, "name": "Model Training", "desc": "Fit LinearRegression / Ridge / Lasso; tune alpha on the VALIDATION split (not k-fold), versioned and registered.", "outputs": "3 trained, registered models"}, {"n": 8, "name": "Model Evaluation", "desc": "Compare on validation; the champion (Ridge) is measured ONCE on the untouched test set. Interpret coefficients for managers.", "outputs": "champion + executive briefing"}]}